Week 4 Assignment
Name: Nicholas Spencer
Date: September 13, 2026

PROGRAM TITLE:
Sneaker Class Program

PROGRAM DESCRIPTION:
This program demonstrates object-oriented programming by creating a Sneaker class.
The class name begins with the letter S because my last name is Spencer.

FILES:
1. objects.py
   - Contains the Sneaker class.
   - The class has three attributes:
     brand
     model
     price
   - The class has two methods:
     apply_discount()
     display_info()
   - The constructor (__init__) is used to assign values to each object.

2. main.py
   - Imports the Sneaker class from objects.py.
   - Creates two Sneaker objects.
   - Displays information about each sneaker.
   - Applies a discount to one sneaker and displays the updated price.

3. Sneaker_UML.png
   - Shows the UML class diagram for the Sneaker class.

OBJECT-ORIENTED CONCEPTS:
Instantiation is demonstrated when sneaker1 and sneaker2 are created from the Sneaker class.
Encapsulation is demonstrated because the brand, model, and price data are grouped together
with the methods that operate on that data inside the Sneaker class.

HOW TO RUN:
Place objects.py and main.py in the same folder.
Run main.py with Python.
